    "created_at": "2024-07-23T14:09:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-07-23T14:09:24Z",
    "body": "A fun hack is to do something like:\r\n\r\n```css\r\nvideo {\r\n  overflow: visible;\r\n  translate: -2000px 0;\r\n\r\n  &::-webkit-media-controls {\r\n    translate: 2000px 0;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat gives you the controls without the video. You still need to draw the video to a canvas before you can filter it. And this hack doesn't work in Firefox.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
